# components.map — what has to happen when ONE component of versions.lock changes.
#
# One component per line, whitespace-separated, five columns:
#
#   name   deps   build   db   restart
#
#   name     must match a name in versions.lock
#   deps     dependency step to rerun after the new source is fetched:
#              npm-ci               npm ci in the component's checkout
#              pip-e:<env>          pip install -e <checkout> into that conda environment
#              conda-update:<env>   conda env update from the component's own
#                                   environment.yml (which ends in "-e .", so it
#                                   reinstalls the package too)
#              -                    nothing
#            <env> is a name from environments.map (today: handler, autoseg).
#   build    next-build | vite-build | -      (config is baked in at build, so the
#            service .env is re-rendered first)
#   db       yes = this component ships the database schema: back up both databases,
#            then run install/db-init.sh (forward migrations only). "-" otherwise.
#   restart  comma-separated systemd units to stop before and start after, or "-"
#
# Read by scripts/upgrade.sh. Every edge below was read from the code at the
# pinned SHAs (2026-11-10), not assumed:
#
#   avrp-gateway       Node service. Owns sql/ (schema, migrations, functions) and
#                      data/db_adapters/sql/ (blob-metadata schema) -> db = yes.
#   avrp-handler       Runs as `python -m src.main` from its checkout in the worker env.
#                      Its two git submodules (automatic_measurement, GoValve-Root-src)
#                      ride along with it: fetch-sources initialises them at the commits
#                      the handler records, so they need no line of their own.
#   segflow4d          Imported IN-PROCESS by the handler (task_manager.py,
#                      study_generator_worker.py) from the worker env. Nothing else loads it.
#   avrp-auto-seg      Its own conda env. The handler never imports it; it starts the
#                      `avrp-auto-seg` program by full path for each task
#                      (helpers/auto_seg_helpers.py). A new version is picked up by the
#                      next task, so no unit restarts.
#   avrp-manager       Next.js; gateway address baked at build.
#   avrp-view-service  Static bundle; gateway address baked at build. The file server
#                      reads from disk on each request, so no unit restarts.
#   avrp-util          Loaded by NO service. Only operator tools live here
#                      (deployment/stage-study.mjs uses Node built-ins only).
#   automatic_measurement
#                      The top-level checkout is loaded by NOTHING: the handler imports
#                      its own nested copy (src/modules/measurements/external/...).
#                      Kept in the lock for now; a change here does not change the
#                      running system. To change the measurement code, move the
#                      submodule pointer in avrp-handler and bump the handler's pin.
#   avrp-ipad          Client app, built on a Mac. Nothing on the server.

avrp-gateway           npm-ci                -           yes  valvescope-gateway
avrp-handler           pip-e:handler         -           -    valvescope-handler
segflow4d              pip-e:handler         -           -    valvescope-handler
avrp-auto-seg          conda-update:autoseg  -           -    -
avrp-manager           npm-ci                next-build  -    valvescope-manager
avrp-view-service      npm-ci                vite-build  -    -
avrp-util              -                     -           -    -
automatic_measurement  -                     -           -    -
avrp-ipad              -                     -           -    -
